# Upstream Git workflow

## Remotes

- `origin` → Fluxa repository
- `upstream` → `https://github.com/chen08209/FlClash.git`

## Branches

Work on `feature/*`, `fix/*`, `refactor/*`, `release/*`. Upstream sync on `sync/flclash-<version>` only — **not** direct large merges on `main`.

## Sync flow

```bash
git fetch upstream
git checkout -b sync/flclash-<version>
git merge upstream/main
```

Then: build, tests, UI, Fluxa features, platform builds. Update `docs/fluxa/upstream.md` (version, commit SHA, date).

## Merge priorities

1. **Keep**: upstream bug/security fixes, core, compatibility, performance.
2. **Evaluate**: upstream UI/state/config — may conflict with Fluxa design.
3. **Never overwrite**: Fluxa branding, UI, node system, single-node import, domain models.

Do not force-overwrite Fluxa changes or break `FluxaNode` / profile abstractions to “make sync easy.”
